ility":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.23632999,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.8,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":80.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Chain Bridge Bancorp, Inc. operates as a bank holding company for Chain Bridge Bank, N.A. that provides a range of commercial and personal banking services in the United States. The company offers deposits, treasury management, payments, loans, commercial lending, residential mortgage financing, consumer loans, trust and estate administration, wealth management, noninterest and interest-bearing checking, money market accounts, residential loans, and asset custody. It also provides other account related services, such as wire transfers, safety deposit box rentals, and lockbox; and mobile deposits, ACH, and bill payment services. Chain Bridge Bancorp, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in McLean, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John J. Brough II, M.B.A. | CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $595,305 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 92 people. Revenue per employee of $598K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $125K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Chain Bridge Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $346M market cap on $55M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -3.4pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","The business throws off $11M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.77\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 24% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.4pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6560133487357215},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 17% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 64% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Chain Bridge Bancorp (NYSE:CBNA) Rating Lowered to Hold at Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/chain-bridge-bancorp-nysecbna-rating-lowered-to-hold-at-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794076734.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (CBNA) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/39/Price-Driven_Insight_from_CBNA_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_110726053401_1794047641.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794047641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Wintrust Financial (NASDAQ:WTFC) and Chain Bridge Bancorp (NYSE:CBNA)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/reviewing-wintrust-financial-nasdaqwtfc-and-chain-bridge-bancorp-nysecbna.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793640533.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Chain Bridge Bancorp, Inc. (CBNA) Reports Q3 Earnings: What Key Metrics Have to Say","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/301789